     "page": 1,
     "text": "Page 4  ##\nRichardson Group Medical Group\n\nDr. Brittany Kelly\nOncology\n\nRe: Juan Thomas (DOB 11/18/1981)\n\nNovember 06, 2025\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nThis letter pertains to Mr. Juan Thomas, who was seen in my practice today. Mr. Thomas is being monitored for his Malignant melanoma, stage II. During his visit, I noted his blood pressure to be 140/93 and his weight at 212 pounds. His overall condition stable, and he continues to do well.\n\nMr. Thomas has a history of Malignant melanoma, stage II, diagnosed on September 16, 2018. He underwent treatment approximately 6.7 years ago, and currently, his melanoma is controlled. Despite this, I noted that Mr. Thomas has been non-compliant with certain aspects of his plan. He has missed two scheduled follow-up appointments, which is concerning given the need for consistent monitoring of his condition.\n\nDespite this, Mr. Thomas maintains an active lifestyle and exercises regularly. He reports running 3-4 times a week, which is an excellent sign of his physical health commitment to maintaining his well-being. \n\nAdditionally, Mr. Thomas has a history of tobacco use, having smoked one pack per day since December 10, 2015. However, he quit smoking on March 9, 2025, and has been honest about his tobacco use history. His alcohol consumption is moderate, with approximately 10 drinks per week.\n\nHis family history is pertinent as his mother had colon cancer, diagnosed at age 51, and she passed away at the age of 57. She is no longer living.\n\nJanuary 24, 2025\n\nOn January 24, 2025, Mr. Thomas was seen again regarding his Malignant melanoma, stage II. His blood pressure at visit was 148/92, and he weighed 217 pounds. Mr. Thomas was doing well at that time.\n\nApril 13, 2024\n\nMr. Thomas was seen on April 13, 2024, also for his Malignant melanoma, stage II. His blood pressure at that visit was 137/85, and he weighed pounds. He was doing well at that time.\n\nJuly 02, 2023\n\nOn July 2, 2023, Mr. Thomas presented with a rash. His blood pressure was 144/83, and he weighed 215 pounds at that visit. He was doing well otherwise.\n\nSeptember 18, 2022\n\nOn September 18, 2022, Mr. Thomas was seen regarding his Malignant melanoma, stage II. His blood pressure was l47/82, and he weighed 216 pounds. His melanoma, stage II, has been stable since his treatment approximately 6.7 years prior.\n\nIn summary, Mr. Juan Thomas continues to manage his Malignant melanoma, stage II, effectively. However, his non-compliance with follow-up appointments is a concern and needs to be addressed to ensure his ongoing care is optimized. \n\nThank you for you"
    },
